FITPACK (Dierckx) — vendored into Tessero
=========================================

Source
------
These C files are an f2c translation of the Fortran FITPACK sources shipped in
scipy 1.17.1 at scipy/interpolate/fitpack/*.f (P. Dierckx's FITPACK; the real*8
"ddierckx" variant prepared for scipy by Pearu Peterson).  scipy 1.17.1 still
builds and calls these Fortran routines as the _dfitpack extension; its smoothing
spline API (splrep s>0, UnivariateSpline, bisplrep, SmoothBivariateSpline,
SmoothSphereBivariateSpline, LSQSphereBivariateSpline, RectBivariateSpline(s>0),
RectSphereBivariateSpline) routes through them.

Why f2c (not a hand C port)
---------------------------
FITPACK's auto-knot smoothing runs a rational p-root iteration (fprati) and a
rank-revealing Givens/Housholder least-squares build (fprank/fpgivs/fprota)
whose results depend on floating-point ACCUMULATION ORDER.  A hand C translation
reorders those sums and diverges 5-17% from scipy at the tie-breaks.  f2c
preserves the Fortran source-level arithmetic order exactly, so the compiled C
is BIT-EXACT (0 ULP) vs scipy's gfortran build across the whole smoothing regime,
active p-iteration included.  See the pkg14 de-risk harnesses.

Translation procedure (reproducible)
------------------------------------
1. Extract scipy-1.17.1/scipy/interpolate/fitpack/*.f.
2. Strip the Fortran-90 `recursive` keyword that scipy added (f2c is an F77
   translator): `sed -E 's/^(\s*)recursive\s+//I'`.  4 files that also use the
   F90 `function ... result(x)` form (dblint, evapol, fprati, splint) were
   rewritten to the F77 `real*8 function` form.
3. f2c -A  (ANSI C output).  f2c built from the barak/f2c github mirror with the
   host gcc (no gfortran / no apt needed).

fitpack_support.c
-----------------
A tiny libf2c shim providing ONLY the intrinsics the smoothing routines
reference: d_sign, pow_dd, and no-op list-directed WRITE stubs (s_wsle/do_lio/
e_wsle — used only in surfit's invalid-input diagnostic branch, ier>=10, which
the PHP facades never reach after validation).  Everything else resolves to
libm.  This keeps the vendored tree self-contained with no libf2c dependency,
mirroring the hand-maintained quadpack.c precedent.

